  {%- when 'listings' -%}
    {%- render 'faq-q', mode: render_mode, id: 'listings-1',
        q: "What makes a good product listing?",
        a: "<p>A strong listing answers the buyer's questions quickly:</p><ul><li>What is it?</li><li>What condition is it in?</li><li>What do I receive?</li><li>What size, colour or specification is it?</li><li>Why might I want it?</li><li>How much is delivery?</li><li>When will it arrive?</li></ul><p>Use accurate titles, useful descriptions and clear photographs.</p>",
        t: "A strong listing answers the buyer's questions quickly: What is it? What condition is it in? What do I receive? What size, colour or specification is it? Why might I want it? How much is delivery? When will it arrive? Use accurate titles, useful descriptions and clear photographs.",
        link_text: "Read the Listings Guide",
        link_url: "/pages/learn-listings-guide" -%}
    {%- render 'faq-q', mode: render_mode, id: 'listings-2',
        q: "Should I use my own photographs?",
        a: "<p>Real, clear photographs are usually worth it, because they show the buyer exactly what they are getting. Some platforms also have rules about stock or edited images, so check the one you are using. eBay, for example, requires listing photos to represent the item accurately and does not allow added marketing text or watermarks in listing images.</p>",
        t: "Real, clear photographs are usually worth it, because they show the buyer exactly what they are getting. Some platforms also have rules about stock or edited images, so check the one you are using. eBay, for example, requires listing photos to represent the item accurately and does not allow added marketing text or watermarks in listing images." -%}
    {%- render 'faq-q', mode: render_mode, id: 'listings-3',
        q: "Should I use AI to edit product photos?",
        a: "<p>AI is useful for cleaning up a background or improving presentation, but the final image still has to represent the real product. Do not create colours, features, quantities or packaging the customer will not actually receive.</p>",
        t: "AI is useful for cleaning up a background or improving presentation, but the final image still has to represent the real product. Do not create colours, features, quantities or packaging the customer will not actually receive." -%}
    {%- render 'faq-q', mode: render_mode, id: 'listings-4',
        q: "My product is not selling. Should I reduce the price immediately?",
        a: "<p>Not automatically. Check your photos, title, keywords, description, price, delivery, competition, and whether you chose the right platform.</p><p>Sometimes the listing needs improving rather than simply getting cheaper.</p>",
        t: "Not automatically. Check your photos, title, keywords, description, price, delivery, competition, and whether you chose the right platform. Sometimes the listing needs improving rather than simply getting cheaper.",
        link_text: "Read the Listings Guide",
        link_url: "/pages/learn-listings-guide" -%}
