  {%- when 'business' -%}
    {%- render 'faq-q', mode: render_mode, id: 'business-1',
        q: "When do I need to tell HMRC about my online selling income?",
        a: "<p>If you are buying or making products with the intention of selling them for profit, HMRC may treat that as trading.</p><p>Current UK guidance says that if your total gross trading income is more than £1,000 in a tax year, you generally need to tell HMRC. The £1,000 is a trading income allowance. It is not a rule saying you only become a business after £1,000 of profit.</p>",
        t: "If you are buying or making products with the intention of selling them for profit, HMRC may treat that as trading. Current UK guidance says that if your total gross trading income is more than £1,000 in a tax year, you generally need to tell HMRC. The £1,000 is a trading income allowance. It is not a rule saying you only become a business after £1,000 of profit.",
        link_text: "Check the guidance on GOV.UK",
        link_url: "https://www.gov.uk/guidance/check-if-you-need-to-tell-hmrc-about-your-income-from-online-platforms" -%}
    {%- render 'faq-q', mode: render_mode, id: 'business-2',
        q: "Is the £1,000 limit based on profit?",
        a: "<p>No. HMRC's guidance refers to gross trading income and receipts before expenses, not simply your profit.</p>",
        t: "No. HMRC's guidance refers to gross trading income and receipts before expenses, not simply your profit." -%}
    {%- render 'faq-q', mode: render_mode, id: 'business-3',
        q: "Should I keep records even when I am small?",
        a: "<p>Yes. Keep records of your sales, income and business costs from the beginning. HMRC expects accurate records even for side-hustle activity.</p>",
        t: "Yes. Keep records of your sales, income and business costs from the beginning. HMRC expects accurate records even for side-hustle activity." -%}
    {%- render 'faq-q', mode: render_mode, id: 'business-4',
        q: "Does GBG provide tax advice?",
        a: "<p>No. We can help you understand the basics of running a product business, but tax and legal decisions depend on your circumstances. Use GOV.UK and HMRC guidance, or speak to a qualified professional where you need to.</p>",
        t: "No. We can help you understand the basics of running a product business, but tax and legal decisions depend on your circumstances. Use GOV.UK and HMRC guidance, or speak to a qualified professional where you need to." -%}
